Temporary verifier workflow remained verifier-only and was excluded from official integration.

## Contract

`GenericGuardianSessionActionCandidate` binds one explicit stable `GameId`, one `GuardianAnomalyKind`, and one existing `GuardianAction`.

`GenericGuardianSessionActionSelector.SelectEligible(...)` fails closed unless all of the following are true:

- workload state is `Active`;
- workload-state confidence is `High`;
- target is one exact capturable running process with a stable `GameId`;
- anomaly family is currently `EvidenceBacked` by `GenericGuardianClassifierSupportCatalog`;
- candidate stable `GameId` matches the exact target after trim/case normalization;
- candidate family exactly matches the classified family;
- candidate action safety is exactly `ActionSafety.LiveSafe`.

`Unknown`, `Fallback`, `UnavailableEvidence`, non-Active states, confidence below High, non-exact/non-capturable targets, wrong workload/family and every non-`LiveSafe` safety class remain ineligible.

The selector preserves caller order and candidate object identity and exposes a genuinely read-only collection. Empty input stays empty. No action is synthesized from an anomaly.

